        "answer": {
          "short": "Mean $=12.55$ hectares; median $=7.5$ hectares.",
          "worked": "The total of the 13 areas is $163.2$ hectares.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Mean}&=\\frac{163.2}{13}\\text{ hectares}\\\\\\text{Mean}&\\approx12.55\\text{ hectares}\\end{align*}$$\n\nIn ascending order, the areas are:\n\n$2.2,\\ 2.3,\\ 2.4,\\ 3.2,\\ 3.6,\\ 5.2,\\ 7.5,\\ 9.0,\\ 11.3,\\ 19.2,\\ 27.6,\\ 28.4,\\ 41.3$.\n\nThere are 13 values, so the median is the seventh value: $7.5$ hectares.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Which do you think is a better measure of centre for the data set? Explain your answer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The median, because the larger suburb areas pull the mean upwards.",
          "worked": "The median of $7.5$ hectares is a better measure of centre. The larger areas, especially $41.3$ hectares, pull the mean upwards. The median is less affected by these large values and better represents a typical suburb area.",
